          "text": "so",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct! We use \"so\" before an adjective."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "such",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. \"Such\" needs a noun."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "very",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. \"Very\" doesn't connect with \"that\" to show consequence."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "too",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "A",
      "explanation": "Usamos \"so\" antes de un adjetivo o adverbio para enfatizar una cualidad que produce un resultado (expresado con \"that\").\n\n---",
